1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
The child wants to climb that slide or the ladder, and you're saying, "Be careful."

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:11,200
What does that mean to the child, "Be careful"? What is the child supposed to do except maybe freeze?

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:21,500
Whereas if you said, "That ladder is quite tall. You need to make sure, you know, you're holding the side railings."

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,500
Now you've given him something very specific to do.

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:31,500
And, you know, they learn through their mistakes. That's the whole thing about risky play and the importance of it.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Instead of saying, "If you run on the road, you'll fall and hurt yourself,"

7
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,000
you say, "You may fall if you run fast on the road and you'll hurt yourself."

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,600
If they don't listen, they'll hurt themselves.

9
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,200
That's the logical consequence that happened.

10
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:53,500
That's how children learn. That's how children can evaluate. That's how children can make choices.